# khub extraction contract: firm-ops@0.3.0

Extract every record the source supports into the envelope below.

- Return one JSON document in the envelope shape and nothing else.
- Use only the types listed, spelled exactly; put each extracted record in entities with its type.
- Fill a field only when the source states it. Leave a field out rather than guess: never invent a value, never write an empty string.
- An enum field takes exactly one of its listed values; a pattern field must match its pattern; a many relation takes a list, a single one takes one target.
- A relation target is the id or an alias of an entity the workspace already holds. khub resolves it exactly and reports what it cannot, never linking by resemblance; never invent an id or guess one from a name.
- Never set the fields listed as supplied; khub writes them.
- Quote the passage a record came from in source. Give confidence from 0 to 1 when a value is uncertain.
- A type that lists body sections takes its prose as Markdown under those ## headings, in that order.

Supplied by khub, never filled: type, created, updated, generated.

## Envelope

```json
{"entities": [{"type": "<type>", "fields": {"<field>": "<value>"}, "relations": {"<predicate>": ["<target>"]}, "body": "<markdown>", "source": "<the passage this came from>", "confidence": 1.0}]}
```

## client

When: an organisation is named that we work with, pitch to, or are introduced to

Id: minted by khub as `slug`; never set it.

| field | kind | required | allowed |
|---|---|---|---|
| status | text |  | one of draft, stable, deprecated; default stable |
| author | text |  |  |
| title | text |  |  |
| description | text |  |  |
| resource | text |  |  |
| tags | list |  |  |
| aliases | list |  |  |
| stale_after | datetime |  | matches `\d{4}-\d{2}-\d{2}[Tt]\d{2}:\d{2}:\d{2}(\.\d+)?([Zz]\|[+-]\d{2}:\d{2})` |
| name | text | ✓ |  |
| industry | text |  |  |
| crm_id | text |  | matches `^[0-9]+$` |
| website | text |  |  |

| relation | to | many | required |
|---|---|---|---|
| related | any | ✓ |  |
| references | any | ✓ |  |
| depends_on | any | ✓ |  |
| partner | partnership |  |  |

